1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Ba6 5. b3 Bb4+ 6. Bd2 Bxd2+ 7. Qxd2 c5 8. Bg2 d5 9. cxd5 exd5 10. Qe3+ Qe7 11. Qxe7+ Kxe7 12. Nc3 Nc6 13. O-O-O Rhd8 14. dxc5 bxc5 15. Nh4 Nd4 16. Rd2 Rac8 17. Kb2 Kf8 18. Rhd1 g5 19. e3 Nb5 20. Nxb5 Bxb5 21. Nf3 Ne4 22. Rc2 f6 23. Ng1 c4 {Diagram [#]} 24. a4 $1 {That this wins for White was only understood by the ex-World Champion later. Anton: 'Dass Weiß damit zum Gewinn abwickelt, ist dem Ex-Weltmeister sicher erst später bewusst geworden.'} Be8 25. Bxe4 dxe4 26. Rxd8 Rxd8 27. Rxc4 Rd1 28. Rc1 Rd2+ (28... Bh5 29. Rxd1 Bxd1 30. a5 $1 )29. Rc2 Rd1 30. Ne2 $1 {Naturally not repeating the position - draw refused. Anton: 'Natürlich keine Zugwiederholung, Remis abgelehnt!'} Rh1 31. Nd4 $1 Rxh2 (31... a5 32. b4 $1 )32. a5 Bd7 33. b4 {The Pawns storm on. Black is helpless, despite the equality in material. The Rook on h2 is a tragic figure. After 40 days thinking time Black was convinced of the hopelessness of his position and gave up. 01.11.96-11.06.99} 1-0

