1. d4 {[%mdl 34953]Myers Morgado Anton} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nf3 b6 4. g3 Bb7 5. Bg2 Be7 6. O-O O-O 7. Re1 {Anton: Because my opponent has played the Queen's Indian defence very successfully for many years, I decided to play this less familiar move over the more popular 7 ?c3.} Qc8 {Tsesarsky} 8. Nc3 Ne4 9. Qc2 f5 10. b3 Nxc3 11. Qxc3 a5 12. a3 Bf6 13. Bb2 Na6 (13... c5 $5 {Morgado} )(13... a4 $5 )(13... d6 $5 {Myers} )14. Qd2 Be4 15. Red1 $1 $146 (15. b4 Qb7 $2 (15... axb4 $5 16. axb4 c6 $8 {Anton} 17. Ne5 Bxg2 18. Kxg2 d6 19. Nd3 $14 )(15... c6 $5 16. Bh3 axb4 17. axb4 Bxf3 18. exf3 Nc7 $11 {Myers} )16. b5 Nb8 17. a4 d6 18. Bh3 Qc8 19. c5 dxc5 20. dxc5 Nd7 (20... Rd8 21. Qc1 Bxb2 22. Qxb2 bxc5 $132 )21. Bxf6 Rxf6 22. c6 Nc5 23. Qb2 $2 (23. Qf4 )(23. Qe3 $14 )Bxf3 24. exf3 Nd3 25. Qb3 Nxe1 26. Rxe1 Qf8 27. Bf1 Qb4 28. Qd1 Qe7 29. Bc4 Rd8 30. Qb3 Rd6 31. f4 h6 32. h4 g6 33. Re5 Kg7 34. Kg2 Kh7 35. Re3 Qe8 36. Qa2 Qg8 37. Re1 Qe8 38. Re2 Qe7 39. Re3 Kg7 40. Qb2 Kh7 41. Qa2 Qe8 42. Qb3 Kg7 43. Qc3 Kf7 44. Re5 Ke7 45. Re2 Qg8 46. Qe3 Rf8 47. Qa3 Kf6 48. Qb2+ Kf7 49. Rxe6 Rxe6 50. Bxe6+ Kxe6 51. Qe5+ Kf7 52. Qxc7+ Kf6 {½-½ Alatortsev,V-Makogonov,V/Tbilisi URS 1937/} )Qb7 (15... c5 $5 )16. Ne1 Bxg2 17. Nxg2 c6 (17... d6 $5 {Morgado} )18. Nf4 Bg5 (18... b5 19. Nh5 {Anton} Be7 20. d5 $36 {Myers} )(18... g6 19. h4 $5 Qc8 20. Rab1 Qe8 21. Kg2 $14 {Myers} )(18... Nc7 $5 )19. d5 $1 {Morgado: Now this break is very strong, and the b2-bishop is strengthened.} cxd5 20. cxd5 Nc5 21. dxe6 dxe6 22. Qe3 $1 {Anton: The Queen moves just one square and its prospects are greatly improved! Now it protects b3, overprotects e5, increases the pressure on the Black pawn on e6, and after b4 will attack the Black pawn on b6.} Rfe8 23. Rac1 Re7 {Palciauskas: An important moment for Black. White was contemplating b4 and ?e5 with a penetration along the c-file. It's clear that the defence will be difficult, but is it impossible? Should Black defend passively by ...?e7, or should he try for complications with 23...e5!?} (23... Rad8 $6 24. Rxd8 Bxd8 $8 (24... Rxd8 $2 25. b4 $1 Bxf4 26. gxf4 Ne4 27. f3 $18 {Myers} )25. b4 axb4 26. axb4 Ne4 27. f3 {Morgado} Bf6 28. Bxf6 Nxf6 29. Qe5 $16 )(23... Nd7 $5 24. Rd6 e5 25. Qd3 Nc5 $1 (25... Nf8 26. Rdc6 $1 Rad8 27. Qxf5 $16 {Myers} )26. Qxf5 {Morgado} Be7 27. Rh6 Qe4 28. Qxe4 Nxe4 29. Re6 Bxa3 30. Bxa3 exf4 31. Rxb6 $36 )(23... Rac8 $6 24. b4 $5 Ne4 25. Rxc8 Qxc8 26. Qxb6 axb4 27. Qxb4 Bxf4 28. gxf4 Nf6 29. Qb5 $16 { Myers} )(23... e5 $5 {Morgado} 24. Bxe5 Bf6 (24... Qf7 25. b4 axb4 (25... Nd7 26. Rc7 Re7 $8 27. Qf3 $16 )26. axb4 Nd7 27. Rc7 Rad8 {Anton} 28. h4 $1 Bxf4 29. Qxf4 $18 {Myers} )(24... Nd7 25. Rc7 Qxc7 26. Bxc7 Rxe3 27. fxe3 Nc5 28. Bxb6 Nxb3 29. Rd7 $16 {Anton} )(24... Qe4 25. Qxe4 fxe4 26. Rd5 Rad8 27. Rxd8 Bxd8 28. Bb2 Nxb3 29. Rc8 $16 {Myers} )25. Rd5 Qf7 26. Qf3 $1 {Morgado} (26. Rcd1 Bxe5 27. Rxe5 Rxe5 28. Qxe5 {Anton} Re8 $5 29. Qd6 $1 Qxb3 30. Kg2 $16 )Bxe5 27. Rxe5 Nxb3 28. Rd1 Nc5 29. Rxe8+ Rxe8 30. Qc6 Rb8 31. Rb1 Nd7 32. h4 $5 $16 )24. Be5 $1 {Morgado: Dominating completely the center, and menacing b3-b4.} Ne4 (24... Qe4 $2 25. Qxe4 Nxe4 26. Rc6 $16 {Morgado} )25. b4 $1 Qa6 (25... axb4 26. axb4 b5 $6 27. f3 Nf6 28. Bd6 Ree8 29. Rc7 $16 {Anton} )26. f3 Qb5 27. Bc7 Nf6 $1 (27... e5 $2 28. fxe4 exf4 29. gxf4 Bh6 30. Qb3+ $5 (30. e5 axb4 31. Qb3+ Kh8 32. Rc4 $16 {Anton} )Kh8 31. Qd5 Qe8 32. exf5 axb4 33. axb4 Rxe2 34. Be5 Qg8 35. Qf3 Rxe5 36. fxe5 Bxc1 37. Rxc1 Qf8 38. e6 $18 {Myers} )(27... Bxf4 $2 28. gxf4 Nf6 $2 29. Bd8 Re8 $2 30. Bxf6 gxf6 31. Rc7 $18 {Morgado} )28. Bd8 $1 (28. Qxb6 $2 Qxb6+ 29. Bxb6 e5 $1 $132 {Anton} )Re8 29. Bxf6 Bxf6 30. Nh5 (30. Rd6 $2 axb4 31. Rxb6 Qe5 32. Qxe5 Bxe5 $132 { Anton} )Bd8 {Palciauskas: Perhaps best? Although the bishop now prevents an entry to c7 and defends the pawn on b6, it no longer defends the vital long diagonal and will be a target for White's rooks on d8 or c7.} (30... Bb2 $5 31. Rc7 Kh8 (31... axb4 $2 32. Nxg7 $1 {Morgado} f4 33. Qxf4 Re7 34. Nxe6 $18 )32. Rdd7 Rg8 (32... Rac8 33. Rxg7 $1 Rxc7 34. Rxc7 Qe5 35. Qxe5+ Bxe5 36. Rb7 Rb8 37. Re7 $18 {Myers} )33. Nf4 $5 (33. Rb7 $5 Rab8 34. Qxe6 Rxb7 35. Rxb7 Re8 36. Re7 Rxe7 37. Qxe7 h6 38. Kf1 $16 {Myers} )Rge8 34. Nd3 Bf6 35. Rf7 Rad8 36. Rxf6 gxf6 37. bxa5 Rd7 38. Rxd7 Qxd7 {Anton} 39. Qxb6 $1 Ra8 40. Kg2 Qd5 41. a4 Qxa5 42. Qxe6 $16 )(30... Qe5 $6 31. Nxf6+ Qxf6 (31... gxf6 32. Qxe5 fxe5 33. b5 $1 $18 {[%csl Rb6,Re6] Myers} )32. b5 Rab8 {Anton} 33. Rd6 $1 h6 34. Rc7 Kh7 35. a4 Rbd8 36. Rxb6 Rd1+ 37. Kg2 Qd4 38. Qxd4 Rxd4 39. Rbb7 $18 {Myers} )(30... axb4 $5 31. Nxf6+ gxf6 32. Rc7 $1 Qe5 (32... bxa3 $4 33. Rdd7 Qb1+ 34. Kg2 f4 35. Rg7+ Kh8 36. Qxf4 {+-} )33. Qxe5 fxe5 34. axb4 Red8 35. Rxd8+ Rxd8 36. Rc6 $16 {Morgado} )(30... e5 $4 31. Nxf6+ gxf6 32. Rc7 Rec8 33. Rcd7 Rf8 34. Qh6 $18 )(30... Ra7 $2 31. Rc8 $1 Rae7 32. Nxf6+ gxf6 33. Rxe8+ Rxe8 34. Rd6 $18 {Myers} )31. Rd6 $1 axb4 (31... Kf7 $2 32. a4 $3 Qxb4 (32... Qxa4 33. Qe5 $1 Bf6 34. Rc7+ $18 )33. Qe5 Bf6 34. Rc7+ Kg6 35. Rxg7+ Bxg7 36. Qxg7+ Kxh5 37. Qxh7+ Kg5 38. Qg7+ Kh5 39. Qf7+ Kh6 (39... Kg5 40. h4+ $18 )40. Rd7 Qe1+ 41. Kg2 Qxe2+ 42. Kh3 $18 {Anton} )(31... e5 $2 32. Rc7 $1 Be7 (32... Bxc7 33. Qg5 $18 )33. a4 Qxb4 34. Qxe5 $18 {Anton} )32. Rxe6 Rf8 (32... Kf7 $2 33. Nxg7 {Anton} Rxe6 34. Nxe6 Qd7 35. Nxd8+ $18 )(32... Rxe6 33. Qxe6+ Kf8 (33... Kh8 34. Rc6 $18 )34. axb4 {Anton} Qxb4 35. Qxf5+ $18 )33. Qd4 Rf7 34. axb4 Bc7 (34... Be7 $5 35. Rc4 Bf8 36. Kf2 Rd7 37. Qc3 Qa6 38. Re5 Qa7 39. Rc6 Rf7 40. Nf4 $18 {Myers} )35. Rcc6 Qa6 {Palciauskas: Black has no serious counterplay and is limited to a passive defence for the rest of the game.} (35... Rd8 36. Qc3 Qd5 37. Nxg7 $1 Bxg3 38. hxg3 Rxg7 39. Kf2 $18 {Myers} )(35... Qa4 36. Qc4 Qd1+ 37. Kg2 Qd7 38. Rf6 Raf8 39. Rxf7 Rxf7 40. b5 $18 {Myers} )36. Qd5 (36. Nf4 $1 Qa1+ (36... Raf8 37. Nd5 $1 Bd8 38. Kg2 h6 39. Rcd6 Kh7 40. Nxb6 $18 )37. Qxa1 Rxa1+ 38. Kg2 Bxf4 39. gxf4 Rb1 40. Re8+ Rf8 41. Rxf8+ Kxf8 42. Rxb6 $18 {Myers} )Rd8 (36... Kf8 $2 37. Rxc7 Rxc7 38. Qd6+ Kf7 39. Qxc7+ Kxe6 40. Nxg7+ Kd5 41. Nxf5 $18 )(36... Qa1+ $2 37. Kg2 Rd8 38. Qc4 b5 39. Qc5 Bxg3 40. Rc8 Rff8 41. Rxd8 Rxd8 42. hxg3 $18 {Myers} )37. Qb3 Qa1+ 38. Kg2 Kf8 39. Qc4 Rd4 (39... Rdd7 40. Nf4 {Anton} g6 41. Nd5 $18 )(39... Qa7 40. b5 $1 Qb8 41. Nf4 Bxf4 42. Rxb6 $18 {Myers} )40. Qb5 Rd8 (40... Qa8 $2 41. Rxc7 Rxc7 42. Qxf5+ $18 {Anton} )41. Re3 (41. Nf4 $1 Bxf4 42. gxf4 Qd4 43. Qxb6 Qxb6 44. Rxb6 Rc7 45. b5 $18 {Myers} )Qa7 (41... g6 42. Rec3 Rdd7 43. Nf6 Rd8 44. Nd5 $1 $18 )(41... f4 42. Rec3 Qa7 43. Nxg7 $1 Rxg7 44. Qf5+ $18 )(41... Qd4 42. Rd3 Qb2 43. Re6 Ra8 44. Rde3 $18 )(41... Qd1 42. Nxg7 Kxg7 43. Rxc7 Rxc7 44. Qe5+ $18 )(41... h6 42. Rce6 Qa8 43. Re7 $1 g6 44. Rxf7+ $18 )(41... Rb8 42. Rce6 Qa8 43. Re7 Rxe7 44. Qxf5+ $18 )42. Rce6 Qb8 43. Nf4 Bxf4 {Palciauskas: The knight on d5 would be too strong. Now White's heavy pieces dominate the centre forcing Black into further exchanges.} 44. gxf4 g6 (44... Rc8 45. Kg3 Rd8 46. Qxb6 Rc7 47. Re8+ Rxe8 48. Rxe8+ Qxe8 49. Qxc7 Kg8 50. Qc4+ Kh8 51. b5 $18 {Myers} )45. Qc4 (45. Qxb6 $1 Qxb6 46. Rxb6 Rd2 47. Rb8+ Kg7 48. b5 $18 {Myers} )Kg7 46. Re7 Rdf8 47. Qd4+ Kh6 (47... Kg8 48. Rxf7 $1 Rxf7 49. Re6 Rf8 50. Rxb6 $18 {Myers} )48. R3e6 b5 49. Qd7 Rxe7 (49... Rd8 50. Qxd8 Qxd8 51. Rxf7 $18 {Anton} )(49... Kg7 50. Kg3 Qa8 51. Qxb5 $18 {Myers} )50. Rxe7 Rh8 51. Qd4 (51. Re5 $1 Qa8 52. Qf7 Qc8 53. Qe7 Qd8 54. Qxd8 Rxd8 55. Rxb5 $18 {Myers} )Kh5 (51... Rg8 52. Qf6 Qxf4 53. h4 Rd8 54. Rf7 $18 )(51... Qf8 52. Rb7 Rg8 53. Qd7 Rh8 54. e4 $18 )52. Kh3 Qf8 53. Rd7 {Palciauskas: Black is in virtual Zugzwang! His Rook cannot move and his Queen must protect the rook and keep an eye on f6. /// Morgado: A very beautiful zugzwang position. /// Anton: Schwarz--im Zugzwang paralysiert--vergisst rechtzeitig aufzugeben.} h6 (53... Kh6 54. Kh4 $1 Rg8 55. Qg1 $18 )(53... g5 54. fxg5 f4 55. Qe4 $18 )54. Rg7 g5 $8 (54... Qd8 55. Qf2 Qf6 56. Qg3 $18 {Bauernmatt} )(54... Rg8 55. Qg1 $1 Rxg7 56. Qg4+ $18 {Bauernmatt} )55. Qe5 Rg8 (55... gxf4 56. e4 fxe3 57. Qg3 $18 {Anton} )56. Rxg8 Qxg8 57. Qxf5 Qc4 58. fxg5 Qh4+ 59. Kg2 (59. Kg2 Qxg5+ 60. Qxg5+ hxg5 61. Kg3 Kg6 62. Kg4 Kf6 63. e4 Ke5 64. Kxg5 {Anton} )1-0

