1. d4 {[%mdl 296]} Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 exd5 5. Bg5 c6 6. Qc2 Na6 7. a3 Nc7 8. e3 Be7 9. Bd3 g6 10. Nge2 Ne6 11. Bh4 Ng7 (11... O-O 12. O-O Re8 13. b4 b6 14. Rfd1 Bb7 15. Qb3 Ng4 $5 $13 {Kelly,B-Hunt,H/British ch 1995} )12. f3 {A flexible move. White´s plan is based in the conservation of the dark squares ?, and the possibility to occupy the center in the future with e3-e4. Una movida flexible. Las blancas basan su plan en la conservación del ? de casillas negras, y en la posibilidad de ocupar el centro en elo futuro mediante e3-e4.} (12. O-O Bf5 13. b4 a6 14. Bxf6 Bxf6 15. a4 Bxd3 16. Qxd3 O-O 17. b5 Ne6 18. bxc6 bxc6 19. Rab1 Qa5 20. Rb7 Rfb8 21. Qb1 $14 {Arnett,D-Bonin,Jay/New York MCC (04) 1994} )O-O (12... Nf5 13. Bf2 c5 $6 (13... O-O )14. g4 Nxd4 15. Nxd4 cxd4 16. Qa4+ Bd7 17. Qxd4 $16 {Tisdall,Jonathan-Garcia,Gildardo/Manila ol (10) 1992/0-1 (52)} )13. O-O Nf5 (13... Re8 14. Bf2 Bd6 15. h3 c5 16. dxc5 Bxc5 17. Nb5 Qe7 18. Nbd4 $14 {Sokolov,Andrey-Stromer,Alexander/Viernheim (08) 1992} )14. Bf2 Nd6 (14... c5 15. dxc5 Bxc5 16. Nd4 $14 )15. b3 $5 $146 {[#] A preventive move against the possible future ?c4. Una movida preventiva contra el posible futuro ?c4} (15. e4 $6 dxe4 16. fxe4 Ng4 $132 )(15. Rae1 {Morgado} Re8 $14 )(15. h3 Nh5 16. e4 Be6 17. e5 Ne8 18. g4 Nhg7 19. f4 f5 20. g5 Nc7 21. Rac1 Bf7 22. Qd2 Nce6 23. Rfd1 b6 24. Bb1 Nh5 $132 {Stepanov,O-Morgado,J/cr Konstantinopolsky Memorial 1995} )Bd7 (15... Nh5 16. e4 Be6 17. e5 Ne8 18. Be3 $40 )16. h3 ({If Si} 16. Kh1 { with the idea of giving the square g1 to the ?f2 con idea de darle la casilla g1 al ?f2} a6 17. e4 Nb5 $5 $13 )Nh5 17. e4 {White has been rather succesful avoiding the exchange of the light squares ?, and now occupying the center. Las blancas obtuvieron algún éxito, ya que impidieron el cambio de los ? de casillas blancas, y ahora ocupan el centro.} Rc8 18. e5 Ne8 19. f4 Nhg7 {Black is prepared to face the thematic advance g2-g4-f5 with f7-f5. besides, they keep the possibility of the break c6-c5. Las negras se han preparado para contrarrestar el avance temático g2-g4-f5 mediante f7-f5. Además, conservan la posibilidad de ruptura con c6-c5.} ({It was also possible También era posible} 19... f5 )({Risky was Arriesgada era} 19... f6 )20. Nd1 ({If Si} 20. g4 f5 $132 )f6 $6 {Too optimistic. Black want to keep the central tension, eventually striking with c6-c5, but white has a big concentration of forces in the center, and it is not possible to concrete it. Demasiado optimista. Las negras desean mantener la tensión central y eventualmente golpear con c6-c5, pero las blancas tienen una gran concentración central de piezas y eso no es posible.} ({Better was directly. Mejor era directamente} 20... f5 $5 )({Or also O también} 20... Bf5 21. Ne3 Bxd3 22. Qxd3 f5 )({Or O} 20... Nc7 21. Ne3 f5 )21. Ne3 Nc7 ({But not Pero no} 21... c5 $2 22. Nxd5 cxd4 23. Qb2 fxe5 24. fxe5 $16 )({Or O bien} 21... fxe5 $6 22. fxe5 (22. dxe5 Nc7 (22... Be6 23. g4 d4 24. Nc4 c5 25. f5 gxf5 26. Nf4 $36 )23. g4 Bh4 $13 (23... d4 24. Nc4 c5 25. a4 $40 (25. Bg3 $13 )))Nf5 23. Nxf5 Bxf5 24. Bxf5 Rxf5 25. Ng3 $40 )22. b4 f5 {It is necessasry to close the center before it is too late! Hay que cerrar el centro antes de que sea demasiado tarde!} ({After Luego de} 22... fxe5 23. dxe5 (23. fxe5 Bg5 24. Qc3 Nge6 25. a4 $14 )a6 (23... b6 $2 24. f5 $1 gxf5 25. Nd4 c5 26. Ndxf5 Nxf5 27. Nxf5 Bb5 28. bxc5 bxc5 29. Bxb5 Nxb5 30. a4 $16 )(23... Ra8 24. Ng4 (24. g4 Bh4 (24... a5 25. bxa5 Rxa5 26. f5 $1 $16 )25. Qc3 (25. Bxh4 Qxh4 26. Kh2 Qh6 27. Rf3 Nge6 $6 (27... Rae8 28. Raf1 Nce6 29. Rg3 Rf7 30. g5 Qh5 31. Ng4 $16 )28. f5 Ng5 29. Rg3 Rae8 30. Qc3 $40 Nf7 31. e6 Nxe6 32. fxe6 Rxe6 33. Nf5 $16 )Bxf2+ 26. Rxf2 Qh4 $13 )(24. Rab1 a5 25. bxa5 Bc8 26. Be1 Bxa3 27. Ng4 $14 )Nce6 25. Nh6+ Kh8 26. Be3 a5 27. Qb3 $13 )(23... Kh8 24. Rab1 b6 $13 )(23... a5 $5 )24. Rae1 $14 )(22... a6 23. Rae1 $40 )(22... a5 23. bxa5 $40 )23. Kh2 {White´s ? is placed where it do not disturb the other pieces. El ? blanco s