1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 d5 4. cxd5 Nxd5 5. e4 Nxc3 6. bxc3 Bg7 7. Bc4 O-O 8. Ne2 Qd7 (8... b6 )9. Rb1 ({is isual es usual} 9. O-O )(9. h4 $5 {is idea of Polugaievsky es idea de Polugaievsky} )Qg4 (9... b6 10. O-O Bb7 11. f3 Nc6 (11... e5 $5 )12. Bb5 $1 (12. Be3 Na5 13. Bb5 c6 14. Bd3 c5 15. Qd2 Rfd8 16. d5 c4 $11 {Derieux,C-Spiridonov,N/Cannes 1996/EXT 98} )Rfd8 13. d5 Qc8 14. Bg5 Bf6 15. Bxf6 exf6 16. Bxc6 Bxc6 17. Qd4 $40 {Azmaiparashvili,Z-Epishin,V/Tallinn 1986/EXT 99} )10. Nf4 Qxd1+ 11. Kxd1 {Until here arrives the Yugoslav Encyclopaedia D, 3rd. edition, page 478/42, indicating small advantage for white. Hasta aquí llega la Enciclopedia Yugoslava D, 3a. edición, página 478/42, indicando leve ventaja para las blancas.} c6 $5 $146 {[%mdl 8]} (11... e6 12. d5 $6 (12. h4 $5 )e5 13. Nd3 c6 14. Be3 b6 15. Bb3 Bb7 16. c4 c5 17. a4 $14 {Hebert-Burger, XI Olympiad, final 1992-95  Hebert-Burger, XI Olympiad, final 1992-95} )12. Ba3 Re8 13. e5 e6 $2 {[%mdl 16384] A strategic important, mistake, because the suares f6 and d6 are weakened, and it obstructs the ?c8. White menace e6 was not so strong to justify these big concesions. Un error estratégico importante, ya que debilita las casillas f6 y d6, y obstruye el ?c8. La amenaza blanca e6 no era tan fuerte para justificar tantas concesiones.} ({Baumbach considered Baumbach consideró} 13... b5 14. Bb3 a5 15. Bc2 (15. e6 f5 )Na6 16. Ke2 $14 )14. Ke2 (14. h4 $5 )(14. Ne2 $5 )b6 15. Bd6 Bf8 (15... Ba6 $2 16. Bxa6 Nxa6 17. c4 $16 )(15... Bb7 $5 )16. Bxf8 Kxf8 17. h4 Ba6 18. Bxa6 Nxa6 19. Nd3 {Correctly played, to disturb the thematic break c6-c5. The following white moves go in this direction. Correctamente jugado, para dificultar la ruptura temática c6-c5. Las siguientes jugadas de las blancas apuntan a este objetivo.} Rac8 (19... c5 $6 20. dxc5 Nxc5 21. Nxc5 bxc5 22. Rb7 $16 )20. Rb3 Rc7 (20... c5 $6 21. Ra3 $16 )21. h5 Kg7 (21... c5 22. Ra3 Nb8 23. dxc5 ({If Si} 23. hxg6 c4 $5 {with artificial fires con fuegos artificiales} 24. Rxh7 cxd3+ 25. Kxd3 Nc6 26. Rh8+ Ke7 27. Rxe8+ Kxe8 28. g7 Ne7 $44 )bxc5 24. hxg6 hxg6 25. Rh4 $40 )22. f4 Nb8 (22... c5 23. Ra3 $40 )23. Nf2 Nd7 24. Ne4 c5 25. hxg6 $1 $16 (25. Nd6 Rd8 26. c4 cxd4 27. hxg6 fxg6 $1 28. Rbh3 Nf8 $11 {Baumbach Baumbach} )fxg6 ({A more active defense was Una defensa más activa era} 25... hxg6 26. Nd6 Rd8 27. c4 $1 cxd4 28. Rbh3 Nc5 (28... Nf8 29. Kd3 $16 {Baumbach} )29. Rh7+ Kf8 30. Rh8+ Ke7 31. Nxf7 Rxh8 32. Rxh8 d3+ )26. Ra3 h5 (26... Re7 $5 )27. Kf3 cxd4 (27... Re7 28. g4 hxg4+ 29. Kxg4 Rb7 30. Kg5 $14 )28. cxd4 Re7 ({A little better was Algo mejor era} 28... a5 29. g4 hxg4+ (29... Rh8 30. gxh5 Rh6 31. Ng5 gxh5 32. f5 $16 )30. Kxg4 Rc2 )29. g4 hxg4+ 30. Kxg4 Rc2 31. Rah3 Nf8 32. Nf6 Kf7 (32... Rg2+ 33. Kf3 Rxa2 34. Rh8 Kf7 35. Rc1 {trasposing traspone} )33. Rh8 Rec7 (33... Rg2+ 34. Kf3 Rxa2 35. Rc1 $1 $18 )34. Nh7 $1 $18 R7c3 (34... Rc8 35. Nxf8 Rxf8 36. R1h7+ Ke8 37. Rxf8+ Kxf8 38. Kg5 $18 {Baumbach} )35. Rxf8+ Kg7 36. Rg1 Rh2 (36... Kxh7 37. Re8 Rxa2 38. Rxe6 Rd3 39. Kg5 $18 )37. Re8 Kxh7 38. Rxe6 Rc7 39. d5 Rf7 40. Kf3 Rxa2 41. Rgxg6 1-0

