1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O b5 6. Bb3 Bb7 7. Re1 Bc5 8. c3 d6 9. d4 Bb6 {} 10. Be3 O-O 11. Nbd2 (11. d5 )h6 {} (11... Nd7 )(11... Qe7 )(11... Re8 )(11... Qb8 )(11... exd4 )12. h3 (12. dxe5 dxe5 13. Bxb6 cxb6 14. Qe2 Nh5 15. g3 Nf6 16. Nf1 Na5 17. Bc2 Nc4 $132 {Arkhamia-Basagic, Subotica 1991} )Nd7 {} (12... Re8 $5 {} 13. d5 Ne7 14. Bxb6 cxb6 15. Bc2 Nd7 {} 16. a4 bxa4 17. Rxa4 b5 18. Ra3 Qb6 $13 )(12... Qd7 13. Bc2 Rae8 14. d5 Ne7 15. Bxb6 cxb6 16. Bd3 Ng6 17. a4 Nf4 18. Bf1 bxa4 19. Qxa4 b5 20. Qb4 Rb8 21. c4 bxc4 22. Qxc4 Ne8 23. Qa4 Qxa4 24. Rxa4 f5 25. Rb4 Nf6 26. g3 Ng6 27. exf5 Ne7 28. Rb6 Bxd5 29. Rxb8 Rxb8 $36 {Kuczynski-Polaczek, Saint John 1988} )(12... exd4 13. cxd4 Nb4 14. Qb1 {} c5 15. a3 Nc6 {} 16. e5 dxe5 {} 17. dxe5 Nd5 18. Ne4 c4 19. Bxb6 Qxb6 20. Bc2 Nce7 21. Nd6 Bc8 22. Be4 Be6 23. Qd1 Rad8 24. Qd2 Nc7 25. Nd4 Ne8 26. Nxe6 fxe6 27. Rad1 $16 { Scuderi-Karlsson, corr. 1987/89} )13. Nf1 (13. Bd5 Rb8 14. a4 exd4 15. cxd4 Nb4 16. Bxb7 Rxb7 17. a5 Ba7 18. d5 Nd3 19. Re2 Qf6 20. Bxa7 Rxa7 21. b3 $13 {Khalifman,Alexander-Malaniuk,Vladimir/Tashkent (02) 1987} )(13. a3 Ne7 (13... Na5 14. Ba2 c5 15. b4 cxb4 16. axb4 Nc6 17. d5 Ne7 18. c4 $14 {Pirumian-Shur G/Azov URS Spartakiad 1991} )14. Ba2 Kh8 15. b4 a5 16. Qc2 axb4 17. axb4 f5 18. dxe5 Bxe3 19. Rxe3 Nxe5 20. Nxe5 dxe5 21. Rae1 $13 {Short,N-Kamsky,G/Linares PCA-m(6) 1994} )(13. d5 Ne7 14. Nf1 f5 15. exf5 Nxf5 16. Bxb6 Nxb6 17. Ne3 Qd7 18. Qd2 a5 19. a3 Nxe3 20. Rxe3 a4 $15 {Ponnuswamy,K-Bakliwal,G/Calcutta op 1996} )Ne7 14. Ng3 c5 $6 (14... exd4 $5 )15. Nh4 $1 {I discovered this move in my Database, as suggested by Beliavsky. After deep analysis, I concluded that it is very strong. A little later, I received the new edition of the Yugoslav Enciclopedia C, and it was there! [Page 391/163], but Beliavsky only put a "!? with attack" Esta jugada figuraba en mi base se datos como sugerencia de Beliavsky. Luego de analizarla detenidamente, llegué a la conclusión de que era muy fuerte. Poco tiempo después, recibí la nueva edición de la Enciclopedia Yugoslava tomo C, y allí ya figuraba! [Página 391/163], aunque Beliavsky sólo la califica con el signo "!? con ataque".} (15. Re2 Qc7 16. Rd2 Nf6 17. Bc2 Rad8 (17... exd4 18. cxd4 Ng6 19. Nh2 Rfe8 20. d5 Ne5 21. Re2 c4 22. Nf5 Bxe3 23. Rxe3 Qc5 24. Rg3 Ng6 25. Qf3 $36 {Oden - Dodderidge, cr EK121 1996} )(17... a5 $5 {b5-b4 Beliavsky} )18. Rc1 Ng6 19. a4 Rfe8 20. d5 c4 21. Bxb6 Qxb6 22. axb5 axb5 23. b3 cxb3 24. Bxb3 Bc8 $13 {Ljubojevic - Beliavsky, Reggio Emilia II 1991} )cxd4 $6 ({Better was Mejor era} 15... Nf6 {and after y luego de} 16. Qf3 c4 (16... cxd4 17. Bxh6 d5 $13 {Bison - Muttoni, corr CAPA Martinez Acosta A Memorial 1998.} )17. Bc2 Ng6 18. Nhf5 d5 19. Rad1 dxe4 20. Nxe4 Nxe4 21. Bxe4 Bxe4 22. Qxe4 exd4 23. Bxd4 Bxd4 24. Rxd4 {white had some advantage, despite they could not win, Dolmatov - Potapov, Elista ch-RUS KO 1997 las blancas tuvieron alguna ventaja, aunque luego no pudierion ganar. Dolmatov - Potapov, Elista ch-RUS KO 1997} )16. cxd4 Nf6 $6 {After this move that defends the ? flank only apparently, black has serious problems. Luego de esta jugada que defiende el flanco rey solamente en apariencia, las negras tienen graves problemas.} ({It was still possible Pudo intentarse todavia} 16... Ba5 {but after pero luego de} 17. Nh5 $1 Kh8 (17... Bxe1 $4 18. Qg4 $18 )18. Qg4 (18. Nxg7 $5 {it would be necessary to analyze deeply the following complicated game Habria que analizar detenidamente la siguiente compleja partida:} Bxe1 19. Ngf5 Nxf5 20. Nxf5 Qf6 21. Bxh6 Bxf2+ 22. Kxf2 Rg8 23. Qh5 Rxg2+ 24. Kxg2 Bxe4+ 25. Kh2 Qxf5 26. Qxf5 Bxf5 27. Rf1 Bg6 28. Bxf7 Kh7 29. Be3 Kg7 30. Bb3 Rh8 $11 {Nemeth - Blasovszky, corr 1994} )g6 19. Bxh6 $16 )17. Qf3 $1 $146 {[%csl Yf6,Yh6][%mdl 136] A strong novelty! Una fuerte novedad!} ({only to equality conduces A la igualdad llevaba} 17. dxe5 dxe5 18. Qxd8 Bxd8 19. f3 Nc6 20. Nhf5 Na5 $11 )({or o bien} 17. Rc1 exd4 18. Bxd4 Bxd4 19. Qxd4 Nc6 20. Qd3 Na5 $14 )Bxd4 ({The more complicated variation was La variante mas compleja era} 17... d5 18. dxe5 (18. Ngf5 Nxf5 19. Nxf5 Nxe4 (19... Kh7 20. dxe5 Nxe4 21. Red1 $16 )20. Bxh6 g6 21. Bxf8 Kxf8 22. Nh6 Ng5 23. Qg3 Bxd4 24. Rxe5 Bxb2 )Nxe4 19. Rad1 Nxg3 20. Qxg3 Bxe3 21. Qxe3 $16 {because white has centralized pieces, and attacks the weakness of d5. ya que las blancas disponen de piezas centralizadas, y acosan la debilidad negra de d5.} )({If Si} 17... a5 {with idea of expelling the ?b3, so it could follow con idea de expulsar el ?b3, entonces podia seguir} 18. dxe5 dxe5 19. Rad1 Qc7 20. Bxb6 (20. Nhf5 Nxf5 21. Nxf5 )(20. Bxh6 $5 a4 )Qxb6 21. Nhf5 Nxf5 22. Nxf5 a4 23. Rd6 Qa5 24. Re3 $1 axb3 25. Rxf6 $3 $18 )(17... exd4 18. Bxh6 $1 $16 {with similar variations to the game. con lineas similares a las de la partida.} )18. Bxh6 $1 {[%mdl 512]} d5 ({It was not good No era buena} 18... Bxb2 {for por} 19. Nhf5 (19. Rad1 Bd4 20. Bg5 Nh7 21. Bxe7 Qxe7 22. Ng6 Qf6 23. Qxf6 Nxf6 24. Nxf8 Kxf8 25. Nf5 Nxe4 26. Nxd4 exd4 27. Rxd4 $16 )Nxf5 20. Nxf5 Bxe4 (20... Bc8 21. Bxg7 Bxa1 22. Bxf8 Kxf8 23. Rxa1 Bxf5 24. Qxf5 $16 )21. Rxe4 Nxe4 22. Bxg7 Qg5 $8 23. Rd1 $1 $16 )(18... Kh7 19. Bg5 Neg8 20. Bxf7 Ne7 $8 21. Be6 $16 )19. Ngf5 Nxf5 (19... dxe4 20. Qg3 Nxf5 21. Nxf5 Nh5 22. Qg4 Bc8 23. Qxh5 Bxf5 24. Qxf5 $18 )20. Nxf5 Ne8 21. Qg3 Kh7 22. Bg5 ({it was always decissive Tambien era decisivo.} 22. Nxd4 gxh6 23. Qxe5 dxe4 24. Rad1 )f6 23. Nxd4 exd4 24. Bd2 ({Stronger than Mas fuerte que} 24. Qh4+ Kg8 25. Bd2 Nd6 26. Bxd5+ Bxd5 27. exd5 Nf5 28. Qe4 Qd7 29. d6 )a5 25. a4 b4 26. Rad1 ({Deciding not to prolong the agony Deciden no prolongar la agonia. Era contundente} 26. Rad1 Kh8 (26... Nc7 27. Bf4 Rf7 28. Rxd4 Ne6 29. Rdd1 Nxf4 30. Qxf4 $18 )27. Qh4+ Kg8 28. exd5 Bxd5 29. Bc2 f5 30. Qxd4 $18 )({it was also winning Tambien ganaba} 26. Qd3 Nc7 27. exd5+ f5 28. Rac1 Nxd5 29. Re5 Qf6 30. Qe2 )1-0

