1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Nxe4 6. d4 b5 7. Bb3 d5 8. dxe5 Be6 9. c3 {Recently 9 ?bd2 has been the rage because of Kasparov's dramatic win over Anand in their PCA-World Championship match (New York) 1995.} (9. Nbd2 Nc5 10. c3 d4 11. Ng5 dxc3 12. Nxe6 fxe6 13. bxc3 Qd3 14. Bc2 $3 Qxc3 15. Nb3 Nxb3 16. Bxb3 Nd4 17. Qg4 Qxa1 18. Bxe6 Rd8 19. Bh6 Qc3 20. Bxg7 Qd3 (20... Bxg7 21. Qh5+ )21. Bxh8 Qg6 22. Bf6 {and White went on to win the endgame.} )Be7 10. Be3 O-O 11. Nbd2 Nxd2 12. Qxd2 Qd7 13. Rad1 Rad8 14. Rfe1 Rfe8 15. Qd3 {This move in conjunction with ?c2 will force Black into weakening his kingside.} g6 16. h3 Na5 17. Nd4 c5 {17. ...Nxb3 18.Nxb3 leaves white in control of c5.} 18. Nxe6 fxe6 19. Bc2 Rf8 20. Bh6 Rf7 21. Qg3 Bf8 22. Be3 (22. Bc1 Bg7 23. h4 Rdf8 )Nc4 23. Bc1 Bg7 24. b3 Nb6 {The purpose of 22 ?e3 ?c4 23 ?c1 followed by 24 b3 was to displace the knight to b6 or gain a tempo, if Black's knight returns to a5. My feeling was that from a5 the knight will return to c6 putting pressure on the e-pawn and supporting the advance...d4.} 25. h4 $1 Rdf8 26. Re2 Qe8 27. h5 gxh5 28. Qh3 Rc7 29. Rd3 d4 {Returning a pawn to bring his pieces into play.} 30. cxd4 Nd5 (30... cxd4 31. Rxd4 Qc8 32. Ba3 )31. dxc5 Rxc5 (31... Nb4 32. Rg3 Kh8 33. Be4 Bxe5 (33... Nd5 34. Bxd5 exd5 35. b4 )(33... Rxc5 34. Be3 Rxe5 35. Bd4 )34. Rg5 Rxc5 35. Bb2 )32. Rg3 Rf4 $5 {[#] Also possible was} (32... Nf4 33. Bxf4 (33. Rxg7+ Kxg7 34. Qg3+ Ng6 35. Ba3 )Rxf4 34. Rg5 h6 35. Rxh5 )33. Rg5 (33. Bxf4 Nxf4 34. Rxg7+ Kxg7 35. Qg3+ Ng6 36. Qg5 Qf8 $14 )Rd4 34. Be3 {Better than} (34. Rxh5 Rd1+ $1 35. Bxd1 Rxc1 36. Re1 Nf4 $11 )Nxe3 35. Qxe3 Rcd5 36. Be4 Rd1+ 37. Kh2 R5d4 38. Qf3 {Also possible was} (38. Rc2 Qd8 39. Rxh5 Rxe4 (39... h6 )40. Qxe4 Rh1+ 41. Kxh1 Qd1+ 42. Kh2 Qxh5+ 43. Kg3 )Kh8 (38... R1d2 39. Rxg7+ Kxg7 40. Qf6+ Kg8 41. Rxd2 Rxd2 42. Qg5+ )(38... h6 39. Rxg7+ Kxg7 40. Qf6+ Kg8 41. Qxh6 Qe7 42. Re3 $18 )39. Rxh5 (39. Rxg7 Kxg7 40. Qf6+ Kg8 41. Re3 Rxe4 42. Rxe4 Rd7 {Is not as clear as 39 ?xh5} )h6 40. Qh3 Qf8 (40... Qf7 41. Rxh6+ Kg8 42. Qg4 Kf8 43. Rxe6 $18 )(40... Rd7 41. Rxh6+ $1 Bxh6 42. Qxh6+ Kg8 43. Re3 Rg7 44. Rg3 Qf7 (44... Rxg3 45. Bh7+ )45. Rh3 $18 )41. Qxe6 Rf1 42. Bf5 {[#] Eliminates the threat of ?f4+ and threatens ?g6. So Black resigns.} (42. Bf5 {A possible continuation could be} Rdd1 43. Qg6 Rh1+ 44. Kg3 Qg8 (44... Kg8 45. Rxh1 Rxh1 46. Qh7+ Kf7 47. e6+ Ke7 48. Rd2 )45. Rxh1 Rxh1 46. e6 $18 )1-0

