1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e3 O-O 5. Bd3 d5 6. Nf3 b6 7. O-O Bb7 8. Bd2 {Black has chosen a very solid line. Normally White plays Las negras han elegido una línea sólida. Normalmente las blancas juegan} (8. a3 Bd6 9. cxd5 {which is heavily analysed and leads to no advantage for White. So I chose a less analysed alternative, though Black has several ways of equalising against it. que ha sido enormemente analizada y conduce a posiciones sin ventaja para las blancas. Por eso elegí una alternativa menos analizada, aunque las negras tenbgan distintos caminos para igualar frente a ella.} )Bd6 {Unusual but logical. Inusual pero logica.} 9. Qe2 (9. Qc2 c5 10. cxd5 exd5 11. Ne5 c4 12. Bf5 Nc6 13. f4 Ne7 14. Bh3 a6 15. Be1 Ng6 16. g4 b5 $13 {Brinck Claussen,B-Mortensen,E/Odense 1980/MCD} )Ne4 $5 10. Rfd1 Nd7 {Filling up the d-file! Llenando la columna ´d´!} 11. Be1 a6 (11... f5 {would have been an interesting alternative, e.g. habría sido una interesante alternativa; por ejemplo} 12. Nb5 Be7 13. Ne5 {which is roughly equal. con rápida igualdad} )12. Ne5 $5 $146 {[%mdl 8]} (12. Rab1 Qe7 13. b4 Nxc3 14. Bxc3 dxc4 15. Bxc4 Nf6 16. Be1 Rfd8 17. Bd3 Ne4 $11 {Malich,B-Barczay,L/Budapest 1978/MCL} )Bxe5 13. dxe5 Qe7 14. f4 Ndc5 {Black could have exchanged on c3 and then c4, but then it is difficult for him to mobilise the Q-side pawn majority, while White has attacking chances. Las negras pudieron cambiar en c3 y luego efectuar c4, pero en ese caso es difícilpara ellas movilizar la mayoría de ? del flanco ?, mientras las blancas conservan chances de ataque.} 15. Nxe4 Nxe4 16. Bxe4 dxe4 {Now the e-file is nearly full! I have a slight preference for White's position, as my bishop is slightly less blocked in than Black's. It can come out via h4. Also the f4-pawn gives White some attacking potential. However, Black can counter on the queenside and try to gain control of the d3-square, so I would hesitate to claim any advantage. Ahora la línea e está casi llena! Tengo una pequeña preferencia por la posición de las blancas, ya que mi ? está levemente menos bloqueado que el de las negras. Puede jugar vía h4. También el ?f4 extra tiene algún potencial de ataque. De todos modos, las negras pueden contar con el flanco dama, y tratar de ganar el control de la casilla d3, de modo que no hesitaría en reclamar alguna ventaja.} 17. Qg4 Qc5 18. Rd4 Rad8 $4 {[%mdl 8192] [#] A blunder allowing a long forcing sequence. Un error grave que permite una larga secuencia forzada.} (18... Rfd8 19. Rad1 Rxd4 20. Rxd4 b5 {would be approximately equal. daría aproximada igualdad} )19. b4 Qc6 20. Bh4 h5 ({Not No} 20... Rxd4 $2 21. Bf6 g6 22. Qg5 Qd7 23. h3 Rd1+ 24. Kh2 {and wins. y gana} )21. Qxh5 $1 {Presumably Black had overlooked the strength of this move. Presumiblemente las negras han subestimado la fuerza de esta jugada.} Rxd4 22. Bf6 Ra8 {Forced! Some alternatives are: Forzado! Algunas alternativas son:} (22... gxf6 23. Qg4+ {and 24.exf6 forcing mate y 24.exf6 forzando mate} (23. Qg4+ Kh8 24. exf6 $18 ))(22... Qd7 23. h3 $1 Ra8 24. Qg5 {and now ...?f8 doesn't help because the queen is blocking d7. y ahora ...?f8 no ayuda debido a que la ? está bloqueando d7.} )(22... Qa4 23. Qg5 Rd1+ 24. Kf2 )(22... Rxc4 23. Qg5 Rc1+ 24. Kf2 {is similar. Other rook moves along the back rank block the king's flight to the queenside. es similar. Otras movidas de ? a lo largo de la primera fila bloquean el vuelo del ? hacia el flanco dama.} )23. Qg5 Kf8 24. Qxg7+ Ke8 25. Qg8+ {Since this is not as devastating as it looks, I investigated Ya que esto no es tan devastador como parece, investigué} (25. exd4 Qxc4 26. Qg8+ Kd7 27. Qxf7+ Kc6 {or first 25 b5, but was unable to find anything clear. o primero 25 b5, pero no pude encontrar nada claro.} )Kd7 26. Qxf7+ Kc8 27. exd4 Kb8 28. Rc1 {Since all Black's moves were forced I was able to analyse this position before playing 19 b4. I always analyse the position resulting from a forcing sequence before playing the first move of it, as just occasionally I change my mind and look for earlier alternatives. At first sight it looks as if White's three extra pawns should guarantee an easy win. But with opposite coloured bishops and queens still on the board, the number of pawns is often less relevant than the relative safety of the kings. Here the black king has found a safe haven, while the black queen and bishop are bearing down the long diagonal towards the white king.  White's queen and bishop are temporarily of little use for defensive purposes, so I had to look closely at 28...Qa4 here, getting in behind the pawns. Rittner tries a tricky alternative. Webb: [#] Since all Black's moves were forced I was able to analyse this position before playing 19 b4. I always analyse the position resulting from a forcing sequence before playing the first move of it, as just occasionally I change my mind and look for earlier alternatives. At first sight it looks as if White's three extra pawns should guarantee an easy win. But with opposite coloured bishops and queens still on the board, the number of pawns is often less relevant than the relative safety of the kings. Here the black king has found a safe haven, while the black queen and bishop are bearing down the long diagonal towards the white king.  White's queen and bishop are temporarily of little use for defensive purposes, so I had to look closely at 28...Qa4 here, getting in behind the pawns. Rittner tries a tricky alternative. [#] Webb: [#] Since all Black's moves were forced I was able to analyse this position before playing 19 b4. I always analyse the position resulting from a forcing sequence before playing the first move of it, as just occasionally I change my mind and look for earlier alternatives. At first sight it looks as if White's three extra pawns should guarantee an easy win. But with opposite coloured bishops and queens still on the board, the number of pawns is often less relevant than the relative safety of the kings. Here the black king has found a safe haven, while the black queen and bishop are bearing down the long diagonal towards the white king.  White's queen and bishop are temporarily of little use for defensive purposes, so I had to look closely at 28...Qa4 here, getting in behind the pawns. Rittner tries a tricky alternative. Como todas las jugadas negras fueron forzadas, pude analizar esta posición antes de jugar 19.b4. Siempre analizo la posición resultante de una variante forzada, aunque ocasilnamente cambio mi forma de pensar y miro alternativas anteriores. A primera vista luce como si los tres ? extra de las blancas les garantizan una fácil victoria. Pero con ? de distinto color en el tablero, la cantidad de ? es a menudo menos relevante que la seguridad relativa de los ?. Aquí el ? negro ha encontrado un paraíso seguro, en tanto la ? y ? negros están apuntando sobre el ? blanco por la diagonal larga.  La ? y ? blancos tienen momentaneamente alguna utilidad para propósitos defensivos, de manera que tuve que considerar mucho aquí 28...?a4, penetrando entre los ?. Rittner intentaba una alternativa tramposa.} e3 (28... Qa4 {I think I intended creo que intentaba} 29. Qxe6 {e.g. por ejemplo} Qa3 ({or} 29... Qxb4 30. Bh4 Qd2 31. Re1 )30. Re1 Qc3 31. Bh4 )29. Qg6 e2 ({Here Aquí} 29... Qa4 {is well met by sería contestada con} 30. Qc2 )30. Kf2 {Having noticed the threat of ...Qxc4. Habiendo tomado nota de la amenaza ...?xc4.} Ka7 31. h4 e1=Q+ {Trying to bluff me into [32.Rxe1 line] but I have a counter-trick. Tratando de introducirme en la línea 32.?xe1 pero dispongo de una ¨contra celada¨} 32. Kxe1 (32. Rxe1 Qxc4 )Rg8 $1 33. d5 $1 (33. Qxg8 {would allow permitiría} Qe4+ {which is nearly perpetual. que es casi jaque perpetuo.} )Rxg6 34. dxc6 Bxc6 35. Rc2 $1 Bxg2 36. f5 exf5 37. h5 Rg3 38. Rxg2 {Because 38...?xg2 39 e6 forces Black to give up his rook for one of the pawns. Porque 38...?xg2 39 e6 fuerza a las negras a entregar su ? por uno de los ?.} 1-0

